    "title": "Facility",
    "excerpt":"UWPR’s state of the art instrumentation and equipment      The Proteomics Resource’s instrument room is located in the basement of 850 Republican St. in ~3500 sq. ft. of lab space.   Instruments   The facility currently houses six mass spectrometers for use by UWPR collaborators:      Astral   Orbitrap Fusion Lumos Tribrid   Orbitrap Fusion Tribrid   Orbitrap Exploris480 1 and 2   TSQ Altis   The facility also offers two types of nano-liquid chromatography and autosampler instruments:      EASY-nLC™ 1200 (qty. 6, for TSQ Altis, Tribrids, and Exploris 480)   Vanquish Neo (qty. 2, for Astral and Exploris 480 only)   The full list, including retired instruments, is on the Instruments page.   Computing Resources   The Proteomics Resource maintains dedicated servers and storage for data processing, described on the Computing Resources page.   For Grant Writers   Additional details of the facility are provided in this Word document intended for grant writing.  ","url": "https://proteomicsresource.washington.edu/facility/"
