    "title": "For MS Laboratories & Cores",
    "excerpt":"Hardware designs and reference material from the UWPR   The UWPR shares the hardware designs, setup guides, and reference material below with other laboratories and core facilities. The parts lists and instructions are free to download, and the hardware can be built from commercially available parts.   Useful Information      Common Mass Spec Background Ions   Mass Spec Background Ions: Repeating Units   LC and Columns      UWPR Pressure Cell: a pressure cell for packing capillary columns and pre-columns.   LC plumbing examples (pdf): plumbing examples from the UWPR LC-MS systems.   Setting up alternate EASY-nLC solvent filters (pdf)   Mass Specs and Sources      UWPR NanoSpray Ionization (NSI) Source: a source design you can build from commercially available parts; parts lists and assembly instructions are free to download.   UWPR N2 switch for low flow applications (pdf)   MS direct infusion line (pdf)  ","url": "https://proteomicsresource.washington.edu/resources/cores/"
