    "title": "UWPR Safety",
    "excerpt":"UWPR and EH&amp;S Resources   UWPR safety guidelines   All UWPR users must read and abide by the safety guidelines.      No food in the lab.   Always wear appropriate clothing and personal protective equipment. Gloves, goggles, and disposable lab coats are available for you to use. If you cannot find them or are unsure what PPE to use, ask us for help.   Do not use any of the equipment unless you have been trained by UWPR personnel.   Review the SOPs before using any chemicals.   Make sure your EH&amp;S training is up to date, including the “Compressed Gas Safety” training required to use the pressure cells. Check the status of your training records at EH&amp;S My Training (UW NetID required).   UW Laboratory Safety Manual      UW Laboratory Safety Manual   Laboratory specific information (pdf)   Laboratory specific emergency information (pdf)   Personal Protective Equipment (PPE)      UW EH&amp;S PPE page   UWPR PPE assessment (docx)   Chemical inventory and SDS search      MyChem (UW NetID required): the UW chemical inventory and MSDS/SDS search   Chemical Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs)   See the UW EH&amp;S chemical SOP templates and guidelines, or contact EH&amp;S at 206-616-3778.   UWPR SOPs                  SOP (pdf)       Covers                       Organic acids       Acetic acid, formic acid, trifluoroacetic acid                 Acetonitrile       Acetonitrile                 Acutely toxic chemicals       Buspirone hydrochloride, caffeine, dithiothreitol (DTT), FlexMix MS standards, iodoacetamide, Pierce calibrator solution, triple quad calibration solution                 Butylamine       Butylamine                 Flammable solvents       Methanol, isopropanol, ethanol                 Fluoranthene       Fluoranthene                 Formamide       Formamide                 Gas cylinders       Compressed gas cylinders                 Hydrochloric acid       Hydrochloric acid                 Irritants       Ammonium carbonate, calcium chloride dihydrate, cesium iodide, Lithisil 829 potassium lithium silicate solution, potassium silicate solution, silica gel                 Irritants 2       Iodoacetic acid, Laemmli sample buffer, PBS (phosphate buffered saline), tyrosine, Ultramark 1621                 Reserpine       Reserpine                 SDS       SDS (sodium dodecyl sulfate)                 Trypsin       Trypsin           Floor plan and fire safety evacuation plan (FSEP)      B59 mass spec lab floor plan (pdf) (also as pptx)   SLU aerial campus evacuation staging locations, buildings C-S (pdf)   2023 FSEP Building D (pdf)   All SLU fire safety evacuation plans (FSEP) (UW NetID required)   UW Accident Prevention Plan   The UW Accident Prevention Plan covers the anticipated occupational hazards that generally apply to employees across the University. It outlines the policies and procedures implemented to reduce or eliminate these hazards.   Laboratory Risk Assessment Tool (Lab R.A.T.)   The Laboratory Risk Assessment Tool (Lab R.A.T.) helps researchers systematically identify and control hazards to reduce the risk of injuries and incidents. The UWPR Lab R.A.T. assessments are in a folder on the shelf next to the flammable cabinet in Brotman B59.   Incident reporting (OARS)   Report any work-related injury or illness to your supervisor as soon as possible. Then report it to Environmental Health and Safety (EH&amp;S) via the Online Accident Reporting System (OARS). Submit the OARS report within 24 hours.   EH&amp;S health and safety resources                  Topic       Links                       Chemical safety       Overview, Chemical SOPs, Chemical waste, MyChem                 Research and lab safety       Overview, Safety manuals, Emergency washing equipment, Compressed gases and cryogens, Sharps safety                 Training       Safety training, Laboratory safety training guide                 Workplace safety       Overview, Incident reporting, PPE           The Report a Concern form allows you to anonymously report any safety concern or potentially hazardous situation before an accident or injury occurs.   Visit the EH&amp;S website for more resources. The Lab Safety Dashboard (PI log-in, UW NetID required) provides lab safety inspection and self-inspection reports.  ","url": "https://proteomicsresource.washington.edu/resources/safety/"
