    "title": "Resources",
    "excerpt":"A reference collection for shotgun (bottom-up) proteomics as we practice it at the UWPR   Knowledgebase: Shotgun Proteomics   Protein identification and quantification strategies: DDA, DIA, targeted acquisition (SRM, PRM), and stable isotope labeling.   Sample Preparation   Protein extraction, separation, and enrichment.   Protein Digestion &amp; Peptide Fractionation   Cleaving proteins into peptides for LC-MS: MS-compatible detergents, digestion kits and enzymes, chemical cleavage, peptide fractionation and enrichment, and peptide cleanup.   Protocols &amp; Methods   Step-by-step bench protocols for sample preparation, digestion, peptide fractionation, and column preparation.   Data Analysis   References for interpreting LC-MS data.   Reagents &amp; Consumables   Part lists, standards, and consumables used on the UWPR systems.   For MS Laboratories &amp; Cores   Hardware designs and reference material from the UWPR: the NSI source, the column-packing pressure cell, and common background ions.   Safety   UWPR safety guidelines, chemical SOPs, and UW EH&amp;S resources.  ","url": "https://proteomicsresource.washington.edu/resources/"
