    "title": "TSQ Altis",
    "excerpt":"Triple Quadrupole Mass Spectrometer      The TSQ Altis is a triple quadrupole mass spectrometer with Active Ion Management (AIM™) ion optics, segmented quadrupoles, and electron multiplier detection.   TSQ Altis, Installed 10/16/2018   Specifications                  Specification       Value                       Mass range       m/z 5 – 2,000                 SRM rate       600 SRMs/sec                 Selectivity       0.2 Da FWHM for high-resolution SRM                 Sensitivity       500,000 : 1           Available scan functions      Collision induced dissociation (CID)   3,000 timed SRMs (T-SRM)   QED-MS/MS (simultaneous quantitation and structural confirmation)   iSRM (intelligent SRM)  ","url": "https://proteomicsresource.washington.edu/facility/instruments/tsqaltis/"
